      "dcDescription": [
        "Outst in Buddhism -ver3, 2006-04 [[Mag]] Buddhist glimpses (2) Buddhist glimpses (3) Buddhist glimpses Mongolia Sculpture: Vita Tara, “the White Savior.” \n\nThe White Tara is depicted with seven eyes, a third vertical eye in the forehead, an eye in each palm, and one in each sole. She is depicted with earrings, throat jewellery, chair band, foot and arm rings. She has her hair set in a ushnisha and her hair loops fall down over her shoulders. A five-leaf crown crowns her head.\n\nāsana: Vita Tara is depicted sitting in a meditation stand (dhyanasana) on a lotustro. \n\nMudra and attributes: She has"
